# Keeps the build context to what the Dockerfile actually copies.
#
# Without this the context carried .git, every node_modules tree and both SPA dist folders — a few
# hundred MB uploaded on every build, host node_modules COPY'd into the SPA stages only to be
# discarded by `npm ci`, and a cache that missed on any git write.
#
# sdk/typescript/rediensiam-web is deliberately NOT excluded: the admin SPA imports it from source
# through a Vite alias, and leaving it out of the context is what made the image build fail while
# the deploy still reported success.

.git
.gitignore

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/bin
**/obj

**/.vite
**/TestResults
**/coverage
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# Local operator state and anything secret-shaped.
deploy/rediensiam/charts
deploy/rediensiam/values*.secret.yaml
deploy/rediensiam/values*.override.yaml
.sonar.env
.sonarqube
*.bak
